### Open House

Last year our 2nd annual open house garnered over 500 attendees, and we hope to bring in even more this year. Open House is scheduled for **Wednesday, March 2nd from 6 - 8 pm, with _all_ our local Robotics teams -- students from grades 4th through 12th including FIRST Robotics [FLL](http://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/fll), [FTC](http://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/ftc) and [FRC](http://www.firstinspires.org/robotics/frc) teams participating! This event is at Bainbridge Island Highschool in the 300 building.** This will be the first time our new robot for this year's [STRONGHOLD](http://www.firstinspires.org/node/3651) game will be unveiled, as well as allow the public to see our design process and learn about the subteams.

![3e7ddb64-df8b-4b13-90c9-3a8680e17de3](../../assets/posts/savethedateopenhousehalfwaypoint/3e7ddb64-df8b-4b13-90c9-3a8680e17de3.png)  

### We're Halfway There

As we close out week three in the build season, FRC teams around the world are reaching the halfway point. In six weeks, we have [our first competition](/event/). Programming and the mechanics have been hard at work to build this year's robot, and we can't wait to show you our efforts at Open House!

![73024d5b-854b-4fe9-84f2-4a3077cf86d8](../../assets/posts/savethedateopenhousehalfwaypoint/73024d5b-854b-4fe9-84f2-4a3077cf86d8.jpg)

**A Symbiotic Relationship:** Our sponsor [NVIDIA](http://www.nvidia.com/page/home.html) sent us t-shirts with their logo on it, and gave us these cool light-up screwdrivers! Check out Erin and Quinn playing with their new toys. Thank you NVIDIA!
